# scenarios/1_basics.books: loaded by ledger_server into 1_basics.db the first time it is picked,
# and again by Start over. Amounts are in cents.
title	1. The basics: money moves between accounts
about	A company's first months, without VAT, after Martin Kleppmann's article. Each arrow is money leaving one account and reaching another; each account's balance is what came in less what went out.
about	Sales is blue: its balance is negative, money the company earned. Food, Payroll and Depreciation are orange: costs. Profit is what Sales brought in less what the costs took.
currency	USD
account	100000	equity	Capital
account	550000	asset	Bank account
account	489000	liability	Credit card
account	613000	expense	Food
account	240000	asset	Furniture
account	400001	asset	Customer 1
account	700000	revenue	Sales
account	620000	expense	Payroll
account	630000	expense	Depreciation
entry	2011-01-03	The founder puts in savings
posting	Capital	-500000
posting	Bank account	500000
entry	2011-01-04	A bagel on the company credit card
posting	Credit card	-500
posting	Food	500
entry	2011-01-05	A chair, paid from the bank account
posting	Bank account	-50000
posting	Furniture	50000
entry	2011-01-31	The credit card bill is paid from the bank
posting	Bank account	-500
posting	Credit card	500
entry	2011-02-07	Sale to customer 1, invoiced at 5,000
posting	Sales	-500000
posting	Customer 1	500000
entry	2011-02-21	Customer 1 pays
posting	Customer 1	-500000
posting	Bank account	500000
entry	2011-03-31	Salaries, paid from the bank
posting	Bank account	-300000
posting	Payroll	300000
entry	2011-12-31	The chair loses a quarter of its value to depreciation
posting	Furniture	-12500
posting	Depreciation	12500
